A||||9||Ken Wittlief||Free New Shocks Woo Hoo!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-10-2001||09:08 AM||||I'm giving my car one last go over before I take it to my favorite garage for its inspection. I notice the bottom of one front shock is a little wet, so I reach behind it and the whole back side is wet with oil. The only thing they will fail you for on shocks is leaking oil, Damn - need new front shocks. They were rusty old yellow "Monroe gas shocks" (nice big label on them).<P>So I call my favorite parts store and ask if they have shocks for a Fiero, and he looks in his computer and says, "yeah, We got Monore gas shocks,  $22 each and they come with a lifetime guarentee!"<P>  "They DO?! excellent cause thats what is on there now and they are leaking"<P>  So I bring the old ones in and get two free replacements   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  the funny part is, the new ones are blue, and there is no sticker on em, and doenst say "Monroe" on em anywhere.<P>  I guess they finally figured out, if you are gonna advertise a lifetime warrenty, its best if you dont have your name on the shock itself! <P>  BTW, my car is at the garage right now. I looked over the inspection list requirements on the wall, and I think I am good on everything, except one. Check engine light is listed as reason to fail the car.<P>  Mine is running rich and the light comes on after 10 to 15 minutes of driving. With any luck it will stay off long enough to pass inspection.<P>  Everyone, think good thoughts for my fiero during this time of trial and evaluation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrgone||05-10-2001||09:35 AM||||put black tape over the light before you take it in||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rob Durham||05-10-2001||09:51 AM||||I have done the black tape and it does work well.<P>Rob||||reg||7
Z||000003||Spektyr||05-10-2001||10:12 AM||||LOL, I hadn't thought of doing that.  What about simply pulling the lightbulb out of the socket?<P>I don't have to pass any inspections, but that damn shift light annoys the hell out of me.  (Don't like electronics telling me how to drive my car.)  Simply pulling the bulb should 'fix' the problem, right?  Or does that set off some sort of other warning light?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-10-2001||10:29 AM||||Removing the bulb shouldnt set anything off.  It would just be as if the bulb burned out, ECM wouldnt/shouldnt care.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-10-2001||11:40 AM||||Here in CA, they disconnect something to make sure a code sets. If no light, you fail.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-10-2001||01:51 PM||||Got my car back during lunch, it passed! <P>Now I can stop playing with brakes and shocks and wiperblades and get into the serious stuff - time to run a compression and vacuum test on the engine and start tearing into it <P>  I think I have an injector that is stuck open  <P>  I think my CAT is full<P>  I know my oil pan needs 2B replaced<P>  I know an exhaust manifold bolt is missing on the front side (BTW anybody know what length and diameter the bolt should be) Dont know yet if its missing or broken off in there.<P>   A/C not working<P>  Radio needs to be pulled and checked out<P>  heater core is holy and bypassed<P>  need to take the rest of the clearcoat off the wheels and polish them<P>  and paint the car<P>   and paint the intake manifold and the valve covers<P>  I figure I paid $1500 for this car, and I have another few hundred in it so far in brakes and misc parts<P>   if I were making payments on a new car they would be $300/month<P>  so if I spend around 300/month on this car over the next year I'll have a little over $5000 in it all together<P>  and a car that will be like new<P>   and no car payments!||||reg||1
