Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-10-2001||04:26 PM||||They replace them, so they have to sell them (ie they dont give you your money back, they give you another pair of shocks - and installation is your problem). The sales guy said Iwas suppose to have the sales slip to get the warrenty, but he could 'work around' it fi I didnt have one.<P>  If they make a stink about it I will make up my own 'sales slip' on a computer at home, still have a dot matrix printer around somewhere that works   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  I do keep every sales slip and piece of paper for all my cars in a filing cabinet in my basement, but these were put on by the previous owner.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
